WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Six drones targeted a U.S. base in Bahrain, ending two months of calm. This is Omni View, episode 237. After that, a presidential vote in Cape Verde, a summit in Manila, and rent marches in Portugal, then a fight over who may buy advanced chips, a cheating confession in South Korea, and a rocket caught on the tower. Bahrain's military told CNBC its air defenses stopped several Iranian aerial attacks short of their targets, while France 24 carried the Islamic Revolutionary

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:35.260
Guard Corps, a branch of Iran's armed forces, saying the weapons were aimed at a United

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:37.980
States radar at the Al-Rifa helicopter base.

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:43.040
No American or Bahrainian authority immediately confirmed that the radar itself was hit.

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:45.380
Sirens were the first since September.

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:49.560
People reported blast near 4 in the morning and again near 630.

00:00:50.140 --> 00:00:54.540
The interior ministry told residents to stay calm and move to the nearest safe place.

00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:58.760
Bahrain hosts the fifth fleet, the U.S. Navy command for the Gulf.

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:06.080
The Guardian quoted Hayat Ibrahim, 65, telling Ajahn's France press this was the return she had hoped was over.

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:10.620
Two days earlier, the same guards said they had struck an early warning radar there.

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:14.540
U.S. Central Command, which runs American operations in the region,

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:19.720
said it shot down two Iranian drones that time, with no casualties and no damage.

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:25.620
CNBC also reported that President Donald Trump has said he might hold off further attacks on Iran.

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:31.080
if Tehran and the Iran-backed Houthis in Yemen offered no new provocations, while

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:36.400
keeping a naval blockade. On that other front, the Saudi-led coalition said it intercepted

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:41.580
two Houthi ballistic missiles fired toward Riyadh, and three drones in the oil-rich eastern

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:47.600
province. France 24 quoted the guards adding that the Strait of Hormuz, the narrow oil route

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:52.260
out of the Gulf, is closed, and that further American force would draw a harsher answer.

00:01:52.940 --> 00:01:57.500
Barrain's foreign ministry said the kingdom will not be an arena for settling scores, and

00:01:57.500 --> 00:01:59.120
holds Iran fully responsible.

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:03.760
The guard's reason is retaliation for what they call hostile U.S. actions.

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:09.580
Barrain's reason is that the shots were stopped, the pattern is hostile, and the firing state

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:10.420
owns the result.

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:15.980
Whether Central Command later confirms damage at that base, or only interceptions is the

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:16.180
check.

00:02:17.185 --> 00:02:21.205
Cape Verde opened the polls with a woman on a presidential ballot for the first time.

00:02:21.205 --> 00:02:27.185
him, Al Jazeera reported. More than 300,000 people could vote, from 8 in the morning until

00:02:27.185 --> 00:02:32.945
6 in the evening, among six candidates. President Jose Maria Nevez wants a second term.

00:02:33.525 --> 00:02:38.405
Joanna Rosa, a former Justice Minister, is the first woman to run since independence in

00:02:38.405 --> 00:02:44.625
1975. A winner needs more than half the vote. If nobody gets that, the top two meet again

00:02:44.625 --> 00:02:50.545
on November 29th. Account is expected in two to three days. Nevez belongs to the African

00:02:50.545 --> 00:02:56.385
party for the independence of Cape Verde. The oldest party, he was Prime Minister for 15 years,

00:02:56.665 --> 00:03:02.705
became President in 2021, and after his party took 37 of 72 parliamentary seats in May,

00:03:03.265 --> 00:03:08.025
he named Francisco Carvalo, then Mayor of the Capitol Priya as Prime Minister.

00:03:08.705 --> 00:03:14.225
Rosa's movement for democracy had governed for 10 years before that election. In this hybrid system,

00:03:14.225 --> 00:03:20.785
the president can veto and mediate. The president does not run the cabinet day to day, about 500,000

00:03:20.785 --> 00:03:26.305
people live on the islands, and more citizens live abroad than at home, mostly in Portugal and the

00:03:26.305 --> 00:03:33.085
United States. Nearly 77,000 of those abroad are registered to vote at embassies. Jobs are scarce,

00:03:33.405 --> 00:03:38.865
so leaving has long been the pressure on the ballot. Roselma Evora, who teaches political science

00:03:38.865 --> 00:03:44.485
in gender studies at the University of Cabo Verde, told the Associated Press that many voters feel

00:03:44.485 --> 00:03:50.145
the political class does not grasp daily life. Rosa argues for a government that lets young people

00:03:50.145 --> 00:03:55.505
build a life on the islands instead of leaving. Nevis argues for a second term that would organize

00:03:55.505 --> 00:04:02.325
a youth summit aimed at the same Exodus. Watch the first count, one candidate over 50% or run off

00:04:02.325 --> 00:04:08.619
three Sundays from now. Manila opened the annual summit of the Association of Southeast Asian nations,

00:04:08.619 --> 00:04:13.579
an 11-country block that wants one market but cannot order its members to comply.

00:04:14.299 --> 00:04:19.419
Al Jazeera put the meetings at November 15th through the 17th, and the membership at nearly

00:04:19.419 --> 00:04:23.699
694 million people, about 8.4% of the world.

00:04:24.339 --> 00:04:29.719
Protesters met the arrivals over the price of basic goods and over PAC's silica, a US-led

00:04:29.719 --> 00:04:32.319
plan for the artificial intelligence supply chain.

00:04:32.919 --> 00:04:37.619
Oil and gas shortfalls from the war on Iran are what import dependent members carried into

00:04:37.619 --> 00:04:43.699
the hall. The Philippines, Vietnam, and Malaysia are among the most exposed. Manila declared

00:04:43.699 --> 00:04:49.099
a national energy emergency in March. Millions of the block's citizens live and work in the Middle

00:04:49.099 --> 00:04:54.939
East. Governments also fear the fighting could reach the strait of Malacca, the tight sea lane between

00:04:54.939 --> 00:05:01.679
Indonesia, Malaysia, and Singapore. Terror rises of 10 to 12.5 percent since President Trump's second

00:05:01.679 --> 00:05:06.759
term have pushed members to trade elsewhere. He is expected at a special sitting with the block

00:05:06.759 --> 00:05:13.519
on November 17th, then at the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation Meeting in China on the 18th and 19th.

00:05:14.159 --> 00:05:18.519
Al Jazeera also named India's Narendra Modi, Canada's Mark Karni,

00:05:18.999 --> 00:05:23.939
Brazil's Luis Ignacio Lula De Silva, the first sitting Brazilian president to visit the

00:05:23.939 --> 00:05:29.739
Philippines and Russia's foreign minister Sergei Lavrov. At sea, China and four members,

00:05:30.079 --> 00:05:36.159
Brunei, Malaysia, the Philippines, and Vietnam, plus Taiwan have disputed waters thought to hold oil

00:05:36.159 --> 00:05:37.639
and gas under the seabed.

00:05:38.399 --> 00:05:40.959
Talks on a code of conduct began in 2005.

00:05:41.679 --> 00:05:44.479
A 2023 pledge was to finish a draft this year.

00:05:45.119 --> 00:05:49.799
At least 10 rounds ran this year, the last in October, with Malaysia in the chair.

00:05:50.499 --> 00:05:53.479
Portugal's cities filled with marches against surging rents.

00:05:53.899 --> 00:05:58.899
The Associated Press called the crowd's tens of thousands, Al Jazeera called them thousands.

00:05:59.619 --> 00:06:02.299
Authorities have started changes meant to bring prices down.

00:06:02.299 --> 00:06:07.819
Marchers told Al Jazeera those changes are not enough. Neither account names a new statute,

00:06:08.119 --> 00:06:13.453
a rent figure, or a date for the next official step. Commerce Secretary Howard Lutnik has

00:06:13.453 --> 00:06:18.293
pressed for a looser version of rules on advanced artificial intelligence chips sold to data centers

00:06:18.293 --> 00:06:25.853
outside China that still serve Chinese firms. The New York Times reported. A site called A201 in southern

00:06:25.853 --> 00:06:30.873
Malaysia is due to open next year with hundreds of millions of dollars in NVIDIA's most advanced

00:06:30.873 --> 00:06:34.553
servers, and to sell that computing power to a Chinese tech giant.

00:06:35.073 --> 00:06:39.553
The Times said the arrangement is legal, and that it steps around a ban on selling those

00:06:39.553 --> 00:06:41.093
chips straight to Chinese companies.

00:06:41.673 --> 00:06:46.653
The operator is a client of Cantor Fitzgerald, the firm Lutnik used to lead and then passed

00:06:46.653 --> 00:06:47.353
to his sons.

00:06:47.793 --> 00:06:50.273
He now writes the rules that would bear on that business.

00:06:50.953 --> 00:06:56.153
Washington already bars cutting-edge chip sales to China, and has argued for much of two years

00:06:56.153 --> 00:06:58.273
over how far to go in Southeast Asia.

00:06:58.273 --> 00:06:59.113
China.

00:06:59.113 --> 00:07:03.713
China hawks in that argument treat a center sitting outside China, but working for Chinese

00:07:03.713 --> 00:07:05.573
firms as a way around the ban.

00:07:06.293 --> 00:07:10.973
Latinx argument is that tighter oversight of sales to international data centers would

00:07:10.973 --> 00:07:16.493
cut what American firms and video among them can sell in Asia, and that the restriction should

00:07:16.493 --> 00:07:17.473
not go that far.

00:07:18.053 --> 00:07:22.873
The time said lawmakers and others inside the administration have criticized that softer touch.

00:07:23.393 --> 00:07:25.613
No date for a finished rule appears in the piece.

00:07:25.613 --> 00:07:31.228
South Korea's top score on the national exam for would-be tax accountants confessed to

00:07:31.228 --> 00:07:33.508
cheating with generative artificial intelligence.

00:07:33.968 --> 00:07:39.448
The Guardian reported, across two sittings in April and July, he missed one question out

00:07:39.448 --> 00:07:40.268
of 160.

00:07:41.028 --> 00:07:45.288
The confession came on Sunday after months of doubt about marks that looked unreal.

00:07:45.908 --> 00:07:51.228
The same report said organizers of the National College Entrance Exam this Thursday now carry

00:07:51.228 --> 00:07:52.128
a sharper risk.

00:07:52.608 --> 00:07:55.148
It did not describe a penalty already handed down.

00:07:55.148 --> 00:08:01.042
known. SpaceX, in news that counts as progress worth knowing, caught starship with the arms

00:08:01.042 --> 00:08:05.942
of the launch tower after the vehicle came back from orbit, a first, the Associated Press

00:08:05.942 --> 00:08:12.122
