00:09:50.795 --> 00:09:56.468
to the climate crisis. To really understand a fight over chip rules, separate the person

00:09:56.468 --> 00:10:01.568
who buys the processor from the person who rents the work it does. What follows is this shows

00:10:01.568 --> 00:10:07.668
own explanation of that mechanism, not a finding copied from today's reporting. Rules of this sort

00:10:07.668 --> 00:10:13.208
usually stick to a sale, who may purchase the physical chip, and which border that box may cross.

00:10:13.208 --> 00:10:18.248
A warehouse of computers in a country allowed to buy them can still sell hours of calculation

00:10:18.248 --> 00:10:21.228
to a customer in a country barred from buying the hardware.

00:10:21.748 --> 00:10:24.988
The machine never moves, the questions and the answers do.

00:10:25.628 --> 00:10:30.408
A tight reading says the paying customer is the real user, so a serious control has to

00:10:30.408 --> 00:10:33.368
read the service contract, not only the shipping label.

00:10:33.928 --> 00:10:38.408
A narrow reading says a legal sale in a legal country should not turn every later cloud

00:10:38.408 --> 00:10:40.148
customer into a sanctions case.

00:10:40.148 --> 00:10:46.208
Next time a draft rule appears, look for one line, does it bind the buyer of the hardware or

00:10:46.208 --> 00:10:52.647
also the customer who pays for the computing time. On the night over Bahrain, France 24 has the

00:10:52.647 --> 00:10:58.487
